            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Saylo 1.3.0</title>
<h1>Saylo 1.3.0</h1>
<pre style="font: 13px -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; white-space: pre-wrap">- Saylo no longer re-asks for Accessibility, microphone, or speech permissions on every launch or after an update — prompts now appear only when a permission is genuinely missing.

- The trigger key (fn) reliably stops a dictation session started from the menu bar, and a duplicate key-event path that could cut sessions short right after they began is gone.

- First-run model downloads now report themselves: pressing the trigger while a model is downloading or loading shows live progress instead of a silent &quot;Preparing speech…&quot;.</pre>
]]></description>
